Description: container compute for a cluster of trusted machines
 Louhi runs containers on the nodes of a cluster the operator owns, in the
 style of ECS and Fargate: a caller describes a task and how many should run,
 never which machine, and Louhi places it, runs it in a hardened Docker
 container, restarts it by its policy, and reports what it sees. It is a
 hosted system on Dannan, the network layer, and signs callers in with Lugh.
 .
 This package holds louhi-node, one node of the cluster, run by louhi.service
 as the louhi system user (a member of the docker group), and louhi-ctl, the
 API from a terminal.
 .
 The service is installed disabled: write the cluster key and configure
 /etc/louhi/config.yaml and /etc/louhi/secrets.yaml, then enable
 louhi.service.
